.TH SDL_ulltoa 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_ulltoa \- Convert an unsigned long long integer into a string.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "char * SDL_ulltoa(unsigned long long value, char *str, int radix);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This requires a radix to specified for string format\[char46] Specifying 10 produces a decimal number, 16 hexadecimal, etc\[char46] Must be in the range of 2 to 36\[char46]
.PP
Note that this function will overflow a buffer if
.BR str
is not large enough to hold the output! It may be safer to use
.BR SDL_snprintf
to clamp output, or
.BR SDL_asprintf
to allocate a buffer\[char46] Otherwise, it doesn\(aqt hurt to allocate much more space than you expect to use (and don\(aqt forget null terminator bytes, etc)\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I value
the unsigned long long integer to convert\[char46]
.TP
.I str
the buffer to write the string into\[char46]
.TP
.I radix
the radix to use for string generation\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns
.BR str \[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_lltoa (3),
.BR SDL_uitoa (3),
.BR SDL_ultoa (3)
